<https://w3id.org/mailo#EHDS_Art52> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The provision governing the trade-secret / access conflict in the health domain, and the one most directly relevant to MAILO's transparency-secrecy tension. Datasets protected by IP rights, trade secrets or regulatory data protection may still be made available for secondary use provided the health data holder identifies and substantiates the protected elements. The health data access body must then take all specific, appropriate and proportionate legal, organisational and technical measures, which may include contractual arrangements, and may refuse access where a serious risk of infringement cannot be addressed satisfactorily. Art.52(3) covers technical measures. The decision chain it leaves to be operationalised runs: protected element, substantiated claim, access scenario, infringement pathway, safeguard, residual risk, permit or conditional permit or refusal. Added in v5.1.0: MAILO had encoded five EHDS articles and omitted this one."@en .
