<https://w3id.org/mailo#PatentClassification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PatentClassification" .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Right_MedicalRecordAccess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Right to Access Medical Records (C-307/22)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPCCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/mailo#Case> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#DataAct_Art17> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The procedural requirements for a request under Chapter V: what the request must specify, and the cross-border route under Art.17(3) by which a public sector body intending to request data from a holder established in another Member State must first notify that Member State's competent authority designated under Art.37, which then examines the request against Art.17.\n\nCORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier entry described Art.17 as 'B2G Data Sharing (Public Emergency)', asserting that governments may require medical AI companies to share health data in a public health emergency. Public emergency is a ground of exceptional need under Art.15, not the subject of Art.17. Art.14 states the obligation itself. The substantive claim about epidemic surveillance AI therefore rested on the wrong provision."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#DesignerTransposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The proposition is inferred across instruments or contexts by the ontology designer and is not held by any court. Must never be cited as case law. Example: the bridge from C-817/19 independent prior review to a GDPR Art.35 DPIA duty."@en .
