<https://w3id.org/mailo#EHDS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "European Health Data Space. Governs primary use (MyHealth@EU, Art.23) and secondary use (HealthData@EU, Art.75) of health data for research, innovation and AI training. Adopted 11 February 2025, published in the OJ on 5 March 2025, in force 26 March 2025; most secondary-use obligations apply from 26 March 2029, with genetic and clinical-trial data from 26 March 2031. All article references were renumbered in v5.1.0 from COM(2022) 197 proposal numbering to the published text."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art22_3> <https://w3id.org/mailo#grantsRight> <https://w3id.org/mailo#Right_ExpressViews> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_TSD_AIAct_Transparency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EHDS Art.52 is now encoded and provides the medical-domain resolution route for this tension: disclosure into a controlled environment under HDAB-imposed safeguards rather than to the requester. Added in v5.1.0."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#EncodingBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Whether an encoded principle states what a court held, or a\n        construct of the ontology designer built on top of it.\n\n        hasPrecedenceLevel records how much weight a holding claims. It cannot\n        answer the prior question of whether the encoded proposition is a\n        holding at all. Keeping the two apart means a reader can query for\n        everything the graph asserts on the designer's own authority."@en .
