<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_Microsoft_Suinno> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SCOPE WARNING: EP 2 671 173 is a 'method and means for browsing by walking' - discovering web search results by physical proximity while walking. It is neither a medical nor an AI patent. The party name (Suinno Mobile & AI Technologies Licensing Oy) contains 'AI', which is the likely reason this case was captured. It should not be counted as a medical-AI patent case."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Amend_AIAct_v4_FRIA_PublicBodies> <https://w3id.org/mailo#versionStartDate> "2027-08-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_10x_NanoString> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SCOPE CORRECTION and UNVERIFIED (v5.1.0). The label 'Spatial Biology AI' and the tag involvesTechnology GenomicDiagnosticAI are not supported: the dispute concerns spatial genomics instrumentation and in-situ detection chemistry, with no AI element identified in the asserted claims. The tag is removed and the inclusion basis moved from DirectSubjectMatter to DomainContext. This is the same failure mode as Hologic v Siemens and Microsoft v Suinno. Separately, no case number is recorded — the only UPC instance without one — and the specific claims about the Court of Appeal's standard of proof and a 2025 settlement have not been verified. Do not cite until checked."@en .
