<https://w3id.org/mailo#EHDS_Art53> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Health data access bodies may grant access to Art.51 data only where processing is necessary for one of the listed purposes: public interest in public and occupational health; policy-making and regulatory activities; official statistics; education and training in the health or care sector; and scientific research related to health or care that contributes to public health or health technology assessment or ensures high quality and safety of healthcare, medicinal products or medical devices.\n\nArt.53(1)(e)(ii) is of first-order importance to MAILO and was previously absent: it expressly names 'training, testing and evaluation of algorithms, INCLUDING IN MEDICAL DEVICES, IN VITRO DIAGNOSTIC MEDICAL DEVICES, AI SYSTEMS AND DIGITAL HEALTH APPLICATIONS' as a permitted secondary-use purpose. This is the express legal pathway for training medical AI on EHDS data, and the point at which the AI Act Art.10 data-governance duties and the EHDS access regime meet. Added in v5.1.0."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v2_GPAIModelObligations> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPAI model provider obligations apply (Title VIII, Arts.51–56)" .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_MDR_AIAct_DualTrack> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Two separate conformity assessment pathways for the same SaMD. MDCG AIB 2025-1 provides a procedural joint-assessment mechanism but does not harmonise the substantive requirement sets."@en .
