<https://w3id.org/mailo#EPO_T1191_19> <https://w3id.org/mailo#hasOutcome> "Technical Board of Appeal 3.5.05, application 08877672.9 (Fundacio Institut Guttmann): computer-implemented meta-learning method predicting personalised neurorehabilitation interventions. Appeal dismissed. Art.56: the mere application of a known machine learning technique to problems in a particular field is a general trend in technology (following T 161/18 point 3.6) and cannot be inventive as such. Art.83: insufficient disclosure - no example training or validation data, no minimum patient number for a meaningful prediction, and no disclosure of the artificial neural networks' topology, activation functions, end conditions or learning mechanism (following T 161/18 point 2); the Board described the disclosure as more like an invitation to a research programme. Separately, late-filed documents AX2-AX8 were not admitted under RPBA Art.12(4) - an evidential admissibility ruling, NOT a plausibility holding."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
