<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_PLD_AIAct_LiabilityGap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "PLD Art.10(4) presumes defectiveness and/or the causal link where the claimant faces excessive difficulty owing to technical or scientific complexity and has demonstrated that the defect or link is probable; Art.10(5) preserves the defendant's right to rebut. AI Act Art.9-compliant risk-management documentation may serve to rebut, but no legislative safe harbour confirms this. CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the presumption was previously attributed to Art.11, which is exemption from liability."@en .
