<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_BlackBox_PatentProtection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SCOPE NOTE added in v5.1.0: the label and comment conflate patent protection with secrecy. A patent REQUIRES disclosure sufficient to rework the invention (EPC Art.83; see T 161/18 and T 1191/19, which refused AI applications for failing exactly that). It is trade-secret protection, not patent protection, that incentivises withholding model weights. The genuine tension here is between keeping a model opaque and the disclosure that patenting it would require. Needs rewriting before it is cited."@en .
