<https://w3id.org/mailo#EPO_G0001_19> <https://w3id.org/mailo#hasOutcome> "Enlarged Board of Appeal, 10 March 2021 (application EP03793825.5, simulation of pedestrian crowd movement through a building). The COMVIK approach of T 641/00 applies to computer-implemented simulations, which are assessed by the same criteria as any other computer-implemented invention. A technical effect going beyond the normal electrical interactions within the computer — a further technical effect — is required to contribute to inventive step, and any further technical use of the simulation output must be at least implied by the claim. Question 2B was answered in the negative: it is NEITHER SUFFICIENT NOR NECESSARY that the simulation is based on technical principles underlying the simulated system." .
