<https://w3id.org/mailo#MDR_Art83> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "MAILO OPERATIONALISATION: continuous monitoring of model drift and performance degradation in deployment populations is the designer's reading of what PMS entails for AI-SaMD. Art.83 requires a post-market surveillance system proportionate to risk class and device type; it does not name drift. Recorded as such in v5.1.0."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art22_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The data subject shall have the RIGHT NOT TO BE SUBJECT to a decision based solely on automated processing, INCLUDING PROFILING, which produces legal effects concerning him or her or similarly significantly affects him or her. CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier text read 'individuals shall not be subject to', stating a flat prohibition. Whether Art.22(1) is a prohibition applying of its own force or a right the data subject must invoke is contested and was not settled by C-634/21 — see the note on P_634_004. The encoding now follows the wording of the provision rather than pre-committing to one reading. The earlier text also omitted profiling and compressed the two-limb effects test."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#InclusionBasis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#TSD_Art2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalArticle> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art22_2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Art.22(1) does not apply where the decision is (a) necessary for entering into or performance of a contract between data subject and controller, (b) authorised by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject and which lays down suitable measures to safeguard rights, freedoms and legitimate interests, or (c) based on the data subject's explicit consent."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Amend_AIAct_v3b_Omnibus_AnnexI_SaMD> <https://w3id.org/mailo#amendmentDescription> "Omnibus VII provisional agreement — Annex I systems (AI embedded in regulated products including medical devices): 2028-08-02. Single joint MDR+AI Act notified body assessment pathway available. Art.9/10/13/14/43 high-risk obligations apply by this date." .
