<https://w3id.org/mailo#EPO_T0161_18> <https://w3id.org/mailo#hasOutcome> "Technical Board of Appeal 3.5.05, 12 May 2020 (Aequivalenter Aortendruck/ARC SEIBERSDORF), application 06804383.5: method of determining cardiac output from a peripheral arterial blood pressure curve using an artificial neural network. The APPLICATION WAS REFUSED (not a granted patent revoked) because the training of the network could not be reworked by the skilled person - neither suitable input data nor at least one suitable training data set was disclosed (Art.83); the claim was also held to lack inventive step for the same reason (Art.56). Leading EPO authority on training-data disclosure for AI inventions, reflected in the 2024 EPO Guidelines and followed in T 1191/19."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_BlackBox_PatentProtection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\r\n        Deep-learning medical AI is inherently opaque (black-box). Patent protection incentivises\r\n        secrecy over model weights. EU AI Act Art.13 and C-817/19 black-box prohibition\r\n        require transparency for high-risk AI systems, creating structural tension with\r\n        commercial IP protection strategies. TSD Art.2 reinforces the secrecy interest;\r\n        TSD Art.5 carve-outs are the only legislative bridge, but their scope is unresolved.\r\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#hasHumanOversightRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/mailo#HumanOversightRecord> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_Dexcom_Abbott> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Continuous glucose monitoring with algorithmic estimation."@en .
