<https://w3id.org/mailo#amendmentProcedureRef> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/mailo#PendingAmendment> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#PendingAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A proposed but not yet adopted amendment to a legislative provision encoded in MAILO. MAILO encodes the numbering of the text currently in force; a PendingAmendment records, separately and explicitly, that a legislative proposal would change or delete that provision. The two are kept apart deliberately: encoding proposal numbering as though it were in force is the failure mode that produced the EHDS renumbering errors corrected in v5.1.0 Round 3."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#P_307_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A patient is entitled to a first copy of his or her medical records free of charge, without having to give reasons, and to a faithful and intelligible reproduction extending to full documents where that is necessary to understand the personal data they contain (Arts.12(5), 15(1) and 15(3) GDPR). CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier text described an 'unconditional' right covering 'all AI-generated diagnostic outputs'. The judgment concerns neither AI nor an unconditional entitlement — Art.15(3) allows a reasonable fee for further copies, and Art.15(4) preserves the rights of others."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#involvesArticle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a CrossFrameworkTension to a provision it turns on. Added in v5.1.0: tensions cited annexes in prose that the ontology did not encode, so nothing connected the claim to the source."@en .
