<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPCA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Agreement on a Unified Patent Court (in force 2023-06-01). Establishes the UPC as a supranational court for infringement and revocation of European patents across contracting states. Key for medtech AI: opt-out strategy, PI threshold ('more likely than not' invalidity standard from 10x v. NanoString CoA), EPO-UPC divergence risk."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_Sanofi_Amgen> <https://w3id.org/mailo#hasStatus> "Active — EPO BoA hearing scheduled 2026-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_Art14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed so that they can be effectively overseen by natural persons during use, including through appropriate human-machine interface tools. Oversight measures aim to prevent or minimise risks to health, safety or fundamental rights, and must enable the person to understand capacities and limitations, remain aware of automation bias, correctly interpret output, disregard or override it, and intervene or stop the system. The complementedBy link to GDPR Art.22(3) should be read subject to the note on that article: the Art.22(3) safeguards attach only to Art.22(2)(a) and (c), so oversight under Art.14 and the data-protection safeguards do not automatically coincide."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#PLD_Art4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PLD Art.4 — Definitions ('product' includes software and AI systems)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#lit_DAOnt_A_Formal_Ontology_for_EU_Data_Act_Compliance_2024_2> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Reuses LKIF-Core + ODRL + DPV. Single-framework analogue of MAILO's multi-framework target." .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#CrossFrameworkTension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CrossFrameworkTension" .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#C_511_18> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "MISSING METADATA (v5.1.0): no ECLI recorded. Not supplied here because it was not verified against a primary source in this pass, and asserting an identifier from memory is the error class that produced the original C-203/22 defect. Add after checking EUR-Lex."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#lit_Communications_Medicine_Nature_2025_Neuro-symbolic_AI> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://www.nature.com/articles/s43856-025-01194-x> .
