<https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art22_3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In the cases referred to in POINTS (a) AND (c) of Art.22(2), the controller shall implement suitable measures to safeguard the data subject's rights, freedoms and legitimate interests, at least the right to obtain human intervention on the controller's part, to express his or her point of view and to contest the decision. CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier text said these safeguards apply whenever an exception applies. They do NOT attach to point (b): where the basis is Union or Member State law, that law must itself lay down suitable measures. The distinction is material for medical AI operating on a national legal basis, where the Art.22(3) triad cannot simply be assumed."@en .
