<https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art22_4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Decisions referred to in Art.22(2) SHALL NOT be based on special categories of personal data referred to in Art.9(1) — which include health data — unless point (a) (explicit consent) or point (g) (substantial public interest) of Art.9(2) applies AND suitable measures to safeguard rights, freedoms and legitimate interests are in place. CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier text described this as 'enhanced protection', which understates a prohibition with two narrow gateways. Given that health data is squarely within Art.9(1), this is one of the most consequential provisions in MAILO's scope, and the earlier phrasing repeated the error class corrected in P_817_004: a prohibition recorded as a graduated safeguard."@en .
