<https://w3id.org/mailo#EPO_G0001_19> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CORRECTED in v5.1.0. The earlier record stated that 'computer-implemented simulation of a technical process is not excluded from patentability (Art.52(2))'. Two errors. First, the Enlarged Board held that whether the SIMULATED system or process is technical is NOT decisive, so framing the holding around simulation of a technical process inverts the point. Second, the decision is an INVENTIVE STEP ruling under the COMVIK approach, not an Art.52(2) exclusion ruling: the eligibility hurdle is passed by any computer implementation and the analysis happens at Art.56. interpretesArticle is corrected from Art.52 to Art.56. Note this is the third instance of the same pattern in MAILO's EPO material — T 0161/18 and T 1191/19 were both attributed to Art.52 when they turn on Arts.83 and 56."@en .
