<https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_Art86> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An affected person subject to a decision taken by a deployer on the basis of the output of a high-risk AI system LISTED IN ANNEX III, excluding systems under point 2, which produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects them adversely in health, safety or fundamental rights, may obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations of the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure and of the main elements of the decision. Art.86(2) disapplies it where Union or national law provides exceptions; Art.86(3) makes it residual to rights available elsewhere in Union law.\n\nSCOPE WARNING added in v5.1.0, and consequential for MAILO's domain: AI-based medical devices are high-risk by the ANNEX I route under Art.6(1), because MDR and IVDR are listed in Annex I Section A and Class IIa/IIb/III devices require third-party conformity assessment. Annex I is not Annex III. Art.86 therefore does NOT confer a right to explanation in respect of a diagnostic or imaging AI device that is high-risk solely as a regulated medical device. It can apply to healthcare AI reaching high-risk status through Annex III point 5, such as systems determining eligibility for publicly funded healthcare services. For the Annex I population, GDPR Art.15(1)(h) and Art.22 carry the explanation duty alone. The previous complementedBy link to GDPR Art.15(1)(h) implied the two operate together across medical AI; it is retained but qualified by this note."@en .
