<https://w3id.org/mailo#lit_DAOnt_A_Formal_Ontology_for_EU_Data_Act_Compliance_2024_2> <https://w3id.org/mailo#relevanceScore> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "MAILO (Medical AI Legal Ontology) is a machine-executable knowledge graph encoding EU regulatory obligations for medical artificial intelligence systems. It formalises eight EU legislative instruments -- the GDPR, MDR, AI Act, Product Liability Directive, EHDS, Data Governance Act, Data Act, and Trade Secrets Directive -- as OWL 2 classes and SHACL shape constraints, grounded in three CJEU judgments on automated decision-making (Ligue des droits humains, SCHUFA Holding, and Dun & Bradstreet Austria). MAILO functions as a deterministic, auditable compliance-verification layer: SHACL NodeShapes validate instance data describing a medical AI system against the encoded legal constraints and produce structured, traceable conformance reports."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#GXDBio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GXD-Bio Corporation (NPE)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art15_1h> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GDPR Art.15(1)(h) — Automated decision-making: existence, logic, significance and consequences"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#RatioDecidendi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ratio Decidendi"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#hasExplanation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links an automated decision system to its actionable explanation for data subjects (C-203/22 P_203_001; GDPR Art.15(1)(h))."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalTest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Multi-factor test established by case law" .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#MDR_Art15> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Manufacturers must designate a person responsible for regulatory compliance (PRRC). For AI-SaMD companies this person must have expertise in medical AI regulation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#MDR_AnnexI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The GSPRs a device must meet. Chapter II section 17 governs electronic programmable systems and software: devices incorporating such systems shall be designed to ensure repeatability, reliability and performance in line with their intended use, software shall be developed and manufactured in accordance with the state of the art taking account of the development lifecycle, risk management including information security, verification and validation. The provision against which AI-specific validation expectations are read. Added in v5.1.0."@en .
