<https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_Art10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Art.10(3): training, validation and testing data sets shall be relevant, sufficiently representative, and, TO THE BEST EXTENT POSSIBLE, free of errors and complete in view of the intended purpose. CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier comment listed 'freedom from errors, completeness' as flat criteria, dropping the qualifier the final text added precisely because absolute error-freedom is unattainable. The distinction matters for any claim that a dataset defect breaches Art.10(3) — including Tension_EHDS_GDPR_OptOut, which asserts that elevated opt-out rates in a clinically significant subpopulation put a dataset in violation. Under the qualified standard that conclusion requires showing the shortfall was avoidable, not merely that it exists."@en .
