<https://w3id.org/mailo#hasResolutionStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Records whether the tension between two frameworks has been resolved by legislation, case law or authoritative guidance. Values in use: 'unresolved' (no authority addresses the conflict), 'partial' (addressed in part, or addressed for an analogous but not identical situation), and 'procedural_only' (an authority routes the conflict to a forum without fixing a substantive outcome, as in C-203/22). This records the state of the law, not the ontology designer's confidence. Declared in v5.1.0 Round 5: the property was in use on tension instances but had never been typed or defined, so its value set was undocumented and unqueryable."@en .
