<https://w3id.org/mailo#DataAct_Art4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Art.4(1): where data is not directly accessible from the connected product, data holders shall make readily available data, and the relevant metadata, available to the user without undue delay, in the same quality as it is available to the data holder, easily, securely, free of charge and in a machine-readable format. Art.4(4): data holders shall not unreasonably impede the user's choices or rights through the structure, design, function or operation of a digital user interface.\n\nArt.4(6)-(8) carry the trade-secret safeguards: trade secrets are disclosed to the user only where the holder and user agree the measures necessary to preserve confidentiality; the holder may withhold or suspend sharing where it demonstrates that it is highly likely to suffer serious economic damage, with notification to the competent authority. This is the Data Act limb of MAILO's trade-secret-against-transparency tension, and it is a qualified withholding right rather than a veto. Scope broadened in v5.1.0: the entry previously covered only paragraphs (6)-(8)."@en .
